  "id": "Compound::DB00757 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Dolasetron is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Dolasetron may influence Cyp2d6 via multiple mechanisms, including direct binding and modulation of enzymatic activity. Specifically, Dolasetron is linked to Wide Complex Tachycardia, which is caused by Propafenone, and both Propafenone and Dolasetron bind to Cyp2d6. Similarly, Dolasetron is associated with Qrs Axis Abnormal and Wenckebach Phenomenon, both of which are influenced by Trospium and Fingolimod, which also bind to Cyp2d6. These pathways highlight a potential role for Cyp2d6 in the metabolic processing of compounds that are indirectly linked to Dolasetron through various physiological effects. The recurring involvement of Cyp2d6 in these pathways suggests a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
